 r.update(mapping_rationale='Both the improper limiting value and its convergence disposition are requested. Direct coverage is the specific SIMPLE improper-integral demand;finite antiderivative work is a component. Separate endpoint and infinite-interval cases,and preserve negative convergent signed integrals.',value_level_scope_decisions=[dict(rule_id='8227:QUAL04',status='within',quoted_value=note,reason='Actual fixed functions are simple powers/linear-root expressions with one infinite or singular endpoint. Each truncated interval avoids all original internal poles. No principal-value cancellation or general convergence theorem is used.'),dict(rule_id='8227:QUAL05',status='within',quoted_value=', '.join(powers),reason='Actual integration powers are rational and none is−1;simple linear powers are integrated before taking the appropriate endpoint limit.')])
 return r
